# Roadmap-as-Files Pattern — Implementation Spec

Hand this whole document to your coding agent with an instruction like:

> Implement this pattern in our repo. Migrate our existing roadmap into it, preserving all current epics/tasks. Build the `scan` script as specified. Don't invent additional fields or structure beyond what's here unless something in our existing roadmap doesn't fit — flag those cases instead of guessing.

---

## 1. Root marker file

Add (or update) `CLAUDE.md` (or `AGENTS.md`, whatever the coding agent convention is) at the project root with a short pointer — the goal is that any agent opening the repo cold finds the roadmap without being told:

```markdown
## Roadmap

Project roadmap, epics, and tasks live in `/roadmap`, not in this file.

- `/roadmap/epics/<NN-epic-slug>/_epic.md` — one epic's scope, status, revision log
- `/roadmap/epics/<NN-epic-slug>/tasks/*.md` — individual tasks, YAML frontmatter + body
- `/roadmap/_registry.md` — GENERATED. Do not hand-edit. Run `roadmap/scan.js` to refresh.
- `/roadmap/_blocked.md` — GENERATED. Dependency/status issues found by the last scan.
- `/roadmap/_archive/` — superseded epics/tasks land here, never deleted.

Before starting work: run the scan, read `_registry.md` to see what's unblocked and
unassigned, then open the specific task file for full context.
```

---

## 2. Folder structure

```
roadmap/
├── epics/
│   ├── 01-auth-system/
│   │   ├── _epic.md
│   │   └── tasks/
│   │       ├── AUTH-01.md
│   │       ├── AUTH-02.md
│   │       └── ...
│   ├── 02-billing/
│   │   ├── _epic.md
│   │   └── tasks/
│   └── ...
├── _registry.md        # generated
├── _blocked.md          # generated
├── scan.js              # or scan.py — the indexer script
└── _archive/
    ├── epics/           # whole epics that were killed/superseded
    └── tasks/           # individual superseded tasks, kept flat, filename = id
```

Epic folders are numbered (`01-`, `02-`...) for stable ordering. Leave gaps (`010-`,
`020-`) if you want to insert epics later without renumbering — with only 5-6 epics
this is optional, but cheap to do now.

