## 3. Frontmatter schemas

### Epic file — `epics/<NN-slug>/_epic.md`

```yaml
---
id: 01-auth-system
title: Auth System
status: in-progress      # planned | scoping | in-progress | blocked | done | superseded
owner: developer-agent   # optional — who's driving this epic right now
created: 2026-08-31
revision: 1               # bump on material scope/direction change
---

## Goal
One paragraph: what this epic delivers and why.

## Scope Notes
What's explicitly in/out. Update this in place — it's the current truth.

## Revision Log
- rev 1 (2026-08-31): initial scope
```

### Task file — `epics/<NN-slug>/tasks/<ID>.md`

```yaml
---
id: AUTH-01
epic: 01-auth-system
title: Implement JWT Login Route
status: todo              # todo | in-progress | blocked | done | superseded
dependencies: []           # list of task ids, e.g. [AUTH-00]
superseded_by: null        # set only when status: superseded
assigned_agent: developer-agent
created: 2026-08-31
---

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] `POST /api/v1/login` returns valid JWT on correct credentials.
- [ ] Returns `401 Unauthorized` on invalid credentials.
- [ ] Tokens expire in 24 hours.

## Technical Context
Use the `jose` library for signing tokens. Secret key from `process.env.JWT_SECRET`.

## Execution Log
*Agent appends progress notes, command outputs, blocker details here. Never delete
prior entries — prepend a date stamp per entry.*
```

**ID convention:** `<EPIC-PREFIX>-<NN>`, prefix is a short stable abbreviation of the
epic (not the folder number, so it survives epic renumbering). Zero-pad to 2 digits;
move to 3 if an epic exceeds 99 tasks.

---

## 4. Handling direction changes (don't edit history — supersede)

- **Task-level pivot:** don't rewrite the task. Set `status: superseded`, add
  `superseded_by: AUTH-07`, leave the file in place (or move to `_archive/tasks/` —
  pick one convention and stick to it; leaving in place is simpler and keeps
  dependency references valid). Create the new task with its own id.
- **Epic-level pivot:** bump `revision` in `_epic.md`, append to `## Revision Log`
  explaining what changed and why, update `## Scope Notes` to reflect current truth.
  Individual tasks still get superseded per the rule above.
- Never silently delete a task or epic file. If something is fully abandoned, set
  `status: superseded` with no replacement and say so in the epic's revision log.

